1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--monolingual-transition","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/monolingual-transition","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/monolingual-transition","sourceHash":"5ec7ab35556236307ad9c8b10720d61261b917a8a784df5e88781a9cc2a1980c","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:53:24.761Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Monolingual Transition","zh":"单语过渡"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The monolingual transition is the shift from using bilingual dictionaries (target language → native language) to monolingual (also known as \"normal\") dictionaries (target language → target language).","zh":"单语过渡是指从使用双语词典（目标语言 → 母语）转向使用单语词典（也称为“普通”词典，目标语言 → 目标语言）的过程。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This forces your brain to think about words in terms of the target language rather than translating to your native language.","zh":"这会促使你的大脑直接用目标语言思考词义，而不是先将其翻译成母语。"}},{"id":"why-it-might-matter","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It (Might) Matter","zh":"它为什么（可能）很重要"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Bilingual dictionaries create a mental shortcut: every target-language word gets mapped to a native-language equivalent. But many words don't translate perfectly, and this mapping can distort your understanding. A monolingual dictionary defines words using the target language itself, which helps you build a more native-like understanding.","zh":"双语词典会在头脑中建立一条捷径：每个目标语言词汇都会对应一个母语词汇。但许多词无法完美翻译，这种对应关系可能会扭曲你的理解。单语词典使用目标语言本身来解释词义，有助于你建立更接近母语者的理解。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This isn't really a problem for languages that are quite related. English and Spanish, despite looking pretty different, have very similar ways of making words. Bilingual dictionaries are perfectly functional for reaching a very high level. Only occasional words (usually slang) require a native language definition. And some dictionaries don't even contain these words.","zh":"对于关系较近的语言，这其实不是什么问题。英语和西班牙语看起来差异很大，但构词方式十分相似。使用双语词典完全可以达到很高的水平。只有偶尔遇到的词（通常是俚语）才需要用母语来解释，而且有些词典甚至根本不收录这些词。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"For less related languages (English and Japanese, for example), it makes more sense. Many basic Japanese words are hard to translate into English. You might see a list of 10-15 English words used to describe a single Japanese word.","zh":"对于关系较远的语言（例如英语和日语），单语过渡就更有意义。许多基础日语词汇很难翻译成英语。你可能会看到用 10 到 15 个英语词来描述一个日语词的情况。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The biggest problem is that dictionaries are verbose and technical. When you're trying to learn a language, that can be incredibly frustrating.","zh":"最大的问题在于，词典的释义往往冗长且专业。学习语言时，这可能让人感到极其沮丧。"}},{"id":"when-to-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Start","zh":"何时开始"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"For closely related languages (Cousin/Similar): consider starting the transition toward the end of Phase 2B, once you can read basic definitions. However, it's not required. Plenty of people have reached high-level fluency without them.","zh":"对于关系较近的语言（近亲语言／相似语言）：当你已经能够读懂基础释义时，可以考虑在阶段 2B 后期开始过渡。不过，这并非必需。许多人没有使用单语词典，也达到了很高的流利程度。"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"For distant languages: wait until Phase 2C or even later into Phase 3. Monolingual definitions in distant languages require substantially more vocabulary to understand, despite being more potentially useful. Bilingual dictionaries aren't <em>bad</em> and will make your beginner-intermediate phases much easier.","zh":"对于距离较远的语言：等到阶段 2C，甚至阶段 3 的后期再开始。虽然单语释义可能更有用，但要理解距离较远语言中的单语释义，需要大得多的词汇量。双语词典并不<em>差</em>，而且会让你的初级至中级阶段轻松许多。"}},{"id":"ai-dictionaries","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"AI Dictionaries","zh":"AI 词典"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Another option that's much easier than a full on monolingual dictionary is asking an AI chatbot. They're often very good at giving simplified explanations of words without being overly technical. Try asking something like this:","zh":"还有一个比直接使用纯粹的单语词典容易得多的选择：询问 AI 聊天机器人。它们通常很擅长以简明而不过度专业的方式解释词语。可以试着这样问："}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p>Can you please explain \"this word or phrase\" to me in simple Italian?</p>","zh":"<p>可以请你用简单的意大利语向我解释“这个词或短语”吗？</p>"}},{"id":"how-to-transition","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Transition","zh":"如何过渡"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The transition is gradual, not sudden:","zh":"这个过渡是循序渐进的，而不是一蹴而就的："}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"en":"Start by checking the monolingual definition <em>first</em>, then falling back to bilingual if needed","zh":"先<em>查看单语释义</em>，必要时再改看双语释义"},{"en":"Add monolingual definitions to your flashcards alongside bilingual ones","zh":"在闪卡中同时加入单语释义和双语释义"},{"en":"Gradually rely more on monolingual definitions","zh":"逐渐更多地依赖单语释义"},{"en":"You've completed the transition when ~90% of your lookups are understood monolingually","zh":"当你约 90% 的查词都能通过单语释义理解时，就完成了过渡"}]},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"技巧"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Don't use monolingual dictionaries for simple concrete nouns (the definitions are often more confusing than a simple translation)","zh":"不要用单语词典查询简单、具体的名词（释义往往比简单的翻译更令人困惑）"},{"en":"Technical and academic terms are also fine to look up bilingually","zh":"技术和学术术语也完全可以使用双语方式查询"},{"en":"The transition takes weeks to months. Be patient.","zh":"过渡需要数周到数月。请保持耐心。"},{"en":"If you don't want to make the transition, then don't!","zh":"如果你不想过渡，那就不必过渡！"}]}],"cards":[]}}]
